<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Why tuning activation matters?</h2>

<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Setup and notation.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider a depth-<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> network with frozen weight matrices <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1},\ldots,W_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1},\ldots,W_{L}</annotation></semantics></math> and elementwise, possibly group-shared, activations <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\ell}(\cdot;\theta_{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\ell}(\cdot;\theta_{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{0}(x)=x,\quad z_{\ell}=W_{\ell}h_{\ell-1}(x),\quad h_{\ell}(x)=\phi_{\ell}(z_{\ell};\theta_{\ell}),\quad F(x)=h_{L}(x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{0}(x)=x,\quad z_{\ell}=W_{\ell}h_{\ell-1}(x),\quad h_{\ell}(x)=\phi_{\ell}(z_{\ell};\theta_{\ell}),\quad F(x)=h_{L}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\ell}\in\mathbb{R}^{p_{\ell}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\ell}\in\mathbb{R}^{p_{\ell}}</annotation></semantics></math> are <em id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">activation parameters</em>. We analyze why adapting <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\theta_{\ell}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\theta_{\ell}\}</annotation></semantics></math> (while freezing <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{W_{\ell}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{W_{\ell}\}</annotation></semantics></math>) is impactful for expressivity, stability, optimization, and generalization.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Functional directions unlocked by activation parameters</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\theta=\{\Delta\theta_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\theta=\{\Delta\theta_{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{L}</annotation></semantics></math> be a small update. By the chain rule,</p>
<table id="A1.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(x;\theta+\Delta\theta)-F(x;\theta)=\sum_{\ell=1}^{L}\underbrace{\frac{\partial F}{\partial h_{\ell}}(x)}_{\Pi_{j=\ell+1}^{L}J_{j}(x)}\cdot\underbrace{\frac{\partial h_{\ell}}{\partial\theta_{\ell}}(x)}_{D_{\ell}(x)\,\Delta\theta_{\ell}}+\mathcal{O}(\|\Delta\theta\|^{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(x;\theta+\Delta\theta)-F(x;\theta)=\sum_{\ell=1}^{L}\underbrace{\frac{\partial F}{\partial h_{\ell}}(x)}_{\Pi_{j=\ell+1}^{L}J_{j}(x)}\cdot\underbrace{\frac{\partial h_{\ell}}{\partial\theta_{\ell}}(x)}_{D_{\ell}(x)\,\Delta\theta_{\ell}}+\mathcal{O}(\|\Delta\theta\|^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We denote</p>
<table id="A1.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{j}(x):=\mathrm{Diag}\!\big(\phi^{\prime}_{j}(z_{j};\theta_{j})\big)\,W_{j}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:2.072em;" width="2.072em"><mi>Diag</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{j}(x):=\mathrm{Diag}\!\big(\phi^{\prime}_{j}(z_{j};\theta_{j})\big)\,W_{j},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A1.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\ell}(x)\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\ell}\times p_{\ell}},\quad[D_{\ell}(x)]_{i,:}=\Big[\frac{\partial\phi_{\ell}(z_{\ell,i};\theta_{\ell})}{\partial\theta_{\ell}}\Big]^{\top}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>:</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\ell}(x)\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\ell}\times p_{\ell}},\quad[D_{\ell}(x)]_{i,:}=\Big[\frac{\partial\phi_{\ell}(z_{\ell,i};\theta_{\ell})}{\partial\theta_{\ell}}\Big]^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Thus the <em id="A1.SS1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">first-order functional change</em> lies in the span</p>
<table id="A1.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta F(\cdot)\ \in\ \mathrm{span}\left\{\,\big(\Pi_{j=\ell+1}^{L}J_{j}(\cdot)\big)\,D_{\ell}(\cdot)\,e_{k}\ :\ 1\leq\ell\leq L,\ 1\leq k\leq p_{\ell}\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">∈</mo><mi>span</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">{</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn> 1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mn> 1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta F(\cdot)\ \in\ \mathrm{span}\left\{\,\big(\Pi_{j=\ell+1}^{L}J_{j}(\cdot)\big)\,D_{\ell}(\cdot)\,e_{k}\ :\ 1\leq\ell\leq L,\ 1\leq k\leq p_{\ell}\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Its intrinsic dimension is at most <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{\ell}p_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{\ell}p_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> (or <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{\ell}G_{\ell}p_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{\ell}G_{\ell}p_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> if parameters are shared across <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> groups). <span id="A1.SS1.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Therefore, activation tuning provides a low-dimensional yet <em id="A1.SS1.p1.5.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">function-space</em> set of directions unavailable if activations are fixed.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Stability and Lipschitz control</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Denote the Lipschitz seminorm of <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\ell}(\cdot;\theta_{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\ell}(\cdot;\theta_{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="A1.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Lip}(\phi_{\ell};\theta_{\ell}):=\sup_{z}\big|\phi^{\prime}_{\ell}(z;\theta_{\ell})\big|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Lip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mi>z</mi></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Lip}(\phi_{\ell};\theta_{\ell}):=\sup_{z}\big|\phi^{\prime}_{\ell}(z;\theta_{\ell})\big|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For each block <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\ell}=\phi_{\ell}\circ W_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\ell}=\phi_{\ell}\circ W_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Lip}(h_{\ell};\theta_{\ell})\ \leq\ \mathrm{Lip}(\phi_{\ell};\theta_{\ell})\,\|W_{\ell}\|_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Lip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Lip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Lip}(h_{\ell};\theta_{\ell})\ \leq\ \mathrm{Lip}(\phi_{\ell};\theta_{\ell})\,\|W_{\ell}\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Hence the network Lipschitz constant satisfies</p>
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Lip}(F;\theta)\ \leq\ \prod_{\ell=1}^{L}\mathrm{Lip}(\phi_{\ell};\theta_{\ell})\,\|W_{\ell}\|_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Lip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.611em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi>Lip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Lip}(F;\theta)\ \leq\ \prod_{\ell=1}^{L}\mathrm{Lip}(\phi_{\ell};\theta_{\ell})\,\|W_{\ell}\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Network-level deviation under activation updates)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the network after changing <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\mapsto\theta+\Delta\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\mapsto\theta+\Delta\theta</annotation></semantics></math>. Then for any <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|F^{\prime}(x)-F(x)\|_{2}\ \leq\ \sum_{\ell=1}^{L}\Big(\prod_{j&gt;\ell}\mathrm{Lip}(h_{j};\theta_{j})\Big)\,\|\Delta\phi_{\ell}(z_{\ell})\|_{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.611em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>Lip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|F^{\prime}(x)-F(x)\|_{2}\ \leq\ \sum_{\ell=1}^{L}\Big(\prod_{j&gt;\ell}\mathrm{Lip}(h_{j};\theta_{j})\Big)\,\|\Delta\phi_{\ell}(z_{\ell})\|_{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where</span></p>
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\phi_{\ell}(z):=\phi_{\ell}(z;\theta_{\ell}+\Delta\theta_{\ell})-\phi_{\ell}(z;\theta_{\ell})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\phi_{\ell}(z):=\phi_{\ell}(z;\theta_{\ell}+\Delta\theta_{\ell})-\phi_{\ell}(z;\theta_{\ell}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta\phi_{\ell}(z_{\ell})\|_{2}\ \leq\ \sup_{z}\|D_{\ell}(z)\|_{2\to 2}\,\|\Delta\theta_{\ell}\|_{2}\,\sqrt{d_{\ell}}\ +\ \mathcal{O}\big(\|\Delta\theta_{\ell}\|_{2}^{2}\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.500em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mi>z</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.722em" rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta\phi_{\ell}(z_{\ell})\|_{2}\ \leq\ \sup_{z}\|D_{\ell}(z)\|_{2\to 2}\,\|\Delta\theta_{\ell}\|_{2}\,\sqrt{d_{\ell}}\ +\ \mathcal{O}\big(\|\Delta\theta_{\ell}\|_{2}^{2}\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consequences.</span> (i) By directly controlling <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Lip}(\phi_{\ell};\theta_{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Lip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Lip}(\phi_{\ell};\theta_{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math> one can regularize the global Lipschitz constant, which enters standard generalization and robustness bounds. (ii) The deviation bound depends linearly (first order) on activation parameters through <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>, enabling fine-grained, stable modulation even with frozen weights.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Gradient flow, Jacobians, and effective rank</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a single block <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=\phi(Wx;\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=\phi(Wx;\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>, the input Jacobian is</p>
<table id="A1.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{x}=\frac{\partial h}{\partial x}=\mathrm{Diag}\!\big(\phi^{\prime}(Wx;\theta)\big)\,W." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:2.072em;" width="2.072em"><mi>Diag</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{x}=\frac{\partial h}{\partial x}=\mathrm{Diag}\!\big(\phi^{\prime}(Wx;\theta)\big)\,W.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Activation parameters change <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{x}</annotation></semantics></math> via <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, thus altering (i) sensitivity to inputs, (ii) conditioning of the layer, and (iii) gradient flow to preceding layers. If <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> is gated (e.g., with a slope/threshold parameter), let <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}(\theta):=\{i:\phi^{\prime}(z_{i};\theta)&gt;0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}(\theta):=\{i:\phi^{\prime}(z_{i};\theta)&gt;0\}</annotation></semantics></math> be the active set. Then</p>
<table id="A1.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Rank(J_{x})\ \leq\ |\mathcal{A}(\theta)|\ \leq\ d." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Rank(J_{x})\ \leq\ |\mathcal{A}(\theta)|\ \leq\ d.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Hence, tuning <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> modulates the effective rank and spectrum of the linearized map <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\ell}J_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\ell}J_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>, improving gradient propagation in deep stacks.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Optimization geometry and the NTK perspective</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vartheta:=(\{W_{\ell}\},\{\theta_{\ell}\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϑ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vartheta:=(\{W_{\ell}\},\{\theta_{\ell}\})</annotation></semantics></math> and write the neural tangent kernel (NTK) <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\vartheta}(x,x^{\prime})=\langle\nabla_{\vartheta}F(x),\nabla_{\vartheta}F(x^{\prime})\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>ϑ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ϑ</mi></msub><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ϑ</mi></msub><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\vartheta}(x,x^{\prime})=\langle\nabla_{\vartheta}F(x),\nabla_{\vartheta}F(x^{\prime})\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>. Decompose</p>
<table id="A1.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\vartheta}(x,x^{\prime})\ =\ K_{WW}(x,x^{\prime})\ +\ K_{\theta\theta}(x,x^{\prime})\ +\ 2K_{W\theta}(x,x^{\prime})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>ϑ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\vartheta}(x,x^{\prime})\ =\ K_{WW}(x,x^{\prime})\ +\ K_{\theta\theta}(x,x^{\prime})\ +\ 2K_{W\theta}(x,x^{\prime}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Using the first-order expansion,</p>
<table id="A1.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta_{\ell}}F(x)=\Big(\Pi_{j&gt;\ell}J_{j}(x)\Big)\,D_{\ell}(x)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta_{\ell}}F(x)=\Big(\Pi_{j&gt;\ell}J_{j}(x)\Big)\,D_{\ell}(x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">so <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\theta\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\theta\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> spans activation-feature directions <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{D_{\ell}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{D_{\ell}\}</annotation></semantics></math> propagated to the output.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmproposition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmproposition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmproposition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Complementarity at initialization)<span id="A1.Thmproposition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmproposition1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.Thmproposition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmproposition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose pre-activations <math id="A1.Thmproposition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> are centered and whitened within groups, and the initial <math id="A1.Thmproposition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> are independent of <math id="A1.Thmproposition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> (with zero-mean entries). Then</span></p>
<table id="A1.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\,K_{W\theta}(x,x^{\prime})=0,\qquad\mathbb{E}\,K_{\vartheta}(x,x^{\prime})=\mathbb{E}\,K_{WW}(x,x^{\prime})+\mathbb{E}\,K_{\theta\theta}(x,x^{\prime})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>ϑ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\,K_{W\theta}(x,x^{\prime})=0,\qquad\mathbb{E}\,K_{\vartheta}(x,x^{\prime})=\mathbb{E}\,K_{WW}(x,x^{\prime})+\mathbb{E}\,K_{\theta\theta}(x,x^{\prime}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5 </span>Curvature control via <math id="A1.SS5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="A1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> be a twice-differentiable loss and denote <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{x}=\partial h/\partial x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">/</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{x}=\partial h/\partial x</annotation></semantics></math>. For block <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=\phi(Wx;\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=\phi(Wx;\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial^{2}h}{\partial x^{2}}=\mathrm{Diag}\!\big(\phi^{\prime\prime}(Wx;\theta)\big)\,[Wx]\,[Wx]^{\top}\odot I." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:2.072em;" width="2.072em"><mi>Diag</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial^{2}h}{\partial x^{2}}=\mathrm{Diag}\!\big(\phi^{\prime\prime}(Wx;\theta)\big)\,[Wx]\,[Wx]^{\top}\odot I.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Hence the input Hessian of the loss obeys</p>
<table id="A1.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}_{x}\mathcal{L}\ =\ J_{x}^{\top}\nabla^{2}_{h}\mathcal{L}\,J_{x}\ +\ \sum_{i}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial h_{i}}\,\frac{\partial^{2}h_{i}}{\partial x^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.555em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}_{x}\mathcal{L}\ =\ J_{x}^{\top}\nabla^{2}_{h}\mathcal{L}\,J_{x}\ +\ \sum_{i}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial h_{i}}\,\frac{\partial^{2}h_{i}}{\partial x^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Tuning <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> therefore changes both the Gauss–Newton part (through <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{x}</annotation></semantics></math>) and the residual curvature term (through <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>), reshaping the local optimization landscape without touching <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.6 </span>Data-aligned gradients and saturation avoidance</h3>

<div id="A1.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let the gradient w.r.t. a preceding weight matrix <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> be</p>
<table id="A1.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{W_{\ell}}\mathcal{L}=\big(\delta_{\ell}\odot\phi^{\prime}_{\ell}(z_{\ell};\theta_{\ell})\big)\,h_{\ell-1}(x)^{\top}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{W_{\ell}}\mathcal{L}=\big(\delta_{\ell}\odot\phi^{\prime}_{\ell}(z_{\ell};\theta_{\ell})\big)\,h_{\ell-1}(x)^{\top},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> is the backpropagated error. Then</p>
<table id="A1.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\,\|\nabla_{W_{\ell}}\mathcal{L}\|_{F}^{2}\ =\ \mathbb{E}\,\big[\|\delta_{\ell}\|_{2}^{2}\,\|h_{\ell-1}\|_{2}^{2}\big]\cdot\mathbb{E}\,\overline{\phi^{\prime}_{\ell}(z_{\ell};\theta_{\ell})^{2}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝔼</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\,\|\nabla_{W_{\ell}}\mathcal{L}\|_{F}^{2}\ =\ \mathbb{E}\,\big[\|\delta_{\ell}\|_{2}^{2}\,\|h_{\ell-1}\|_{2}^{2}\big]\cdot\mathbb{E}\,\overline{\phi^{\prime}_{\ell}(z_{\ell};\theta_{\ell})^{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where the overline denotes the average across units. Choosing <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> to <em id="A1.SS6.p1.3.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">maximize derivative mass</em> under the moments of <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> keeps most units responsive (not saturated), improving gradient signal-to-noise without changing <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.7 </span>Generalization via capacity control</h3>

<div id="A1.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Define the hypothesis class <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> with frozen <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{W_{\ell}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{W_{\ell}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and activation parameters bounded by <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\theta_{\ell}\|\leq\rho_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\theta_{\ell}\|\leq\rho_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> and local Lipschitz budgets <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Lip}(\phi_{\ell};\theta_{\ell})\leq\lambda_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Lip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Lip}(\phi_{\ell};\theta_{\ell})\leq\lambda_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>. Using standard Lipschitz-based complexity bounds, for inputs <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x\|\leq R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x\|\leq R</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> samples,</p>
<table id="A1.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{R}_{N}(\mathcal{F})\ \lesssim\ \frac{R}{\sqrt{N}}\cdot\Bigg(\sum_{\ell=1}^{L}\Big(\prod_{j&gt;\ell}\lambda_{j}\|W_{j}\|_{2}\Big)\cdot c_{\ell}(\rho_{\ell})\,\|W_{\ell}\|_{2}\Bigg)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℜ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≲</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>R</mi><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{R}_{N}(\mathcal{F})\ \lesssim\ \frac{R}{\sqrt{N}}\cdot\Bigg(\sum_{\ell=1}^{L}\Big(\prod_{j&gt;\ell}\lambda_{j}\|W_{j}\|_{2}\Big)\cdot c_{\ell}(\rho_{\ell})\,\|W_{\ell}\|_{2}\Bigg),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS7.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\ell}(\rho_{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\ell}(\rho_{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math> is a polynomial-in-<math id="A1.SS7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> constant induced by the chosen parametrization of <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Takeaways.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Functional expressivity at low cost.</span> Activation parameters open a low-dimensional <em id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">function-space</em> of directions (Eq. <a href="#A1.E13" title="In A.1 Functional directions unlocked by activation parameters ‣ Appendix A Why tuning activation matters? ‣ Don’t Forget the Nonlinearity: Unlocking Activation Functions in Efficient Fine-Tuning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stable, controllable modulation.</span> Activation Lipschitz and curvature (<math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{\prime},\phi^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{\prime},\phi^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>) yield explicit network-level deviation and robustness control (Eqs. <a href="#A1.E16" title="In A.2 Stability and Lipschitz control ‣ Appendix A Why tuning activation matters? ‣ Don’t Forget the Nonlinearity: Unlocking Activation Functions in Efficient Fine-Tuning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>, <a href="#A1.E17" title="In Theorem A.1 (Network-level deviation under activation updates). ‣ A.2 Stability and Lipschitz control ‣ Appendix A Why tuning activation matters? ‣ Don’t Forget the Nonlinearity: Unlocking Activation Functions in Efficient Fine-Tuning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>, <a href="#A1.E26" title="In A.5 Curvature control via ϕ^′ and ϕ^′′ ‣ Appendix A Why tuning activation matters? ‣ Don’t Forget the Nonlinearity: Unlocking Activation Functions in Efficient Fine-Tuning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Better conditioning and gradient flow.</span> By changing gates/slopes, activation tuning controls Jacobian rank/spectrum and mitigates saturation (Eqs. <a href="#A1.E20" title="In A.3 Gradient flow, Jacobians, and effective rank ‣ Appendix A Why tuning activation matters? ‣ Don’t Forget the Nonlinearity: Unlocking Activation Functions in Efficient Fine-Tuning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>, <a href="#A1.E21" title="In A.3 Gradient flow, Jacobians, and effective rank ‣ Appendix A Why tuning activation matters? ‣ Don’t Forget the Nonlinearity: Unlocking Activation Functions in Efficient Fine-Tuning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>, <a href="#A1.E28" title="In A.6 Data-aligned gradients and saturation avoidance ‣ Appendix A Why tuning activation matters? ‣ Don’t Forget the Nonlinearity: Unlocking Activation Functions in Efficient Fine-Tuning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Complementary optimization geometry.</span> Activation-parameter gradients contribute an NTK component largely orthogonal (in expectation) to weight-only directions (Eqs. <a href="#A1.E22" title="In A.4 Optimization geometry and the NTK perspective ‣ Appendix A Why tuning activation matters? ‣ Don’t Forget the Nonlinearity: Unlocking Activation Functions in Efficient Fine-Tuning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>, <a href="#A1.E23" title="In A.4 Optimization geometry and the NTK perspective ‣ Appendix A Why tuning activation matters? ‣ Don’t Forget the Nonlinearity: Unlocking Activation Functions in Efficient Fine-Tuning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>, <a href="#A1.E24" title="In Proposition A.1 (Complementarity at initialization). ‣ A.4 Optimization geometry and the NTK perspective ‣ Appendix A Why tuning activation matters? ‣ Don’t Forget the Nonlinearity: Unlocking Activation Functions in Efficient Fine-Tuning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">These results justify <em id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">activation tuning</em> as a principled and effective axis for adapting pretrained models, independently of the particular parameterization chosen for <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Why rational function?</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Rational functions offer a compact and flexible parametrization that can <em id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">uniformly approximate</em> the activation functions used in modern networks—both smooth (e.g., <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tanh" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>tanh</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tanh</annotation></semantics></math>, sigmoid, GELU/erf-based, SiLU/Swish) and non-smooth (e.g., ReLU, Leaky/ReLU)—on any bounded pre-activation domain. We record the key facts concisely.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Definition.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A degree-<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m,n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m,n)</annotation></semantics></math> rational function is</p>
<table id="A2.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{m,n}(x)\;=\;\frac{P_{m}(x)}{Q_{n}(x)}\;=\;\frac{\sum_{i=0}^{m}a_{i}x^{i}}{\sum_{j=0}^{n}b_{j}x^{j}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{m,n}(x)\;=\;\frac{P_{m}(x)}{Q_{n}(x)}\;=\;\frac{\sum_{i=0}^{m}a_{i}x^{i}}{\sum_{j=0}^{n}b_{j}x^{j}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and we assume the domain <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\subset\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\subset\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is compact with a pole-free margin</p>
<table id="A2.E31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\inf_{x\in K}\,|Q_{n}(x)|\;\geq\;\gamma\;&gt;\;0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">inf</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.558em">&gt;</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\inf_{x\in K}\,|Q_{n}(x)|\;\geq\;\gamma\;&gt;\;0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">which is standard for stable approximation on <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Density on compact sets.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Because polynomials are dense in <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(K)</annotation></semantics></math> (Stone–Weierstrass) and polynomials are a special case of rationals (take <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{n}\equiv 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{n}\equiv 1</annotation></semantics></math>), rationals are also dense:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A2.E32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E32.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\forall f\in C(K),\ \forall\varepsilon&gt;0,\ \exists\ m,n,\ \exists\,r_{m,n}\ \text{s.t.}\ \sup_{x\in K}|f(x)-r_{m,n}(x)|\ &lt;\ \varepsilon." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mo rspace="0.667em">∃</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mo rspace="0.337em">∃</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mtext>s.t.</mtext><munder><mo lspace="0.667em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></munder><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.389em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo rspace="0.778em">&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall f\in C(K),\ \forall\varepsilon&gt;0,\ \exists\ m,n,\ \exists\,r_{m,n}\ \text{s.t.}\ \sup_{x\in K}|f(x)-r_{m,n}(x)|\ &lt;\ \varepsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Thus any continuous activation used in practice admits uniform rational approximations on bounded pre-activation ranges.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Fast rates for smooth activations.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is real-analytic on a neighborhood of <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> (typical for sigmoid/<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tanh" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>tanh</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tanh</annotation></semantics></math>/erf-like activations), best rational approximants achieve geometric convergence:</p>
<table id="A2.E33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exists\ C&gt;0,\ \rho&gt;1:\quad\inf_{\deg(r)\leq N}\ \sup_{x\in K}|f(x)-r(x)|\ \leq\ C\,\rho^{-N}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">∃</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.0835em">inf</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.0835em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exists\ C&gt;0,\ \rho&gt;1:\quad\inf_{\deg(r)\leq N}\ \sup_{x\in K}|f(x)-r(x)|\ \leq\ C\,\rho^{-N},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=m+n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=m+n</annotation></semantics></math> is total degree. This is substantially faster than the algebraic rates of many polynomial schemes.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Near-root-exponential rates for kinks.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For non-smooth activations with a finite number of kinks (e.g., ReLU, <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|x|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|x|</annotation></semantics></math>), rational approximation still excels:</p>
<table id="A2.E34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exists\ C,c&gt;0:\quad\inf_{\deg(r)\leq N}\ \sup_{x\in K}|f(x)-r(x)|\ \leq\ C\,\exp\!\big(-c\,\sqrt{N}\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">∃</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.0835em">inf</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.0835em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exists\ C,c&gt;0:\quad\inf_{\deg(r)\leq N}\ \sup_{x\in K}|f(x)-r(x)|\ \leq\ C\,\exp\!\big(-c\,\sqrt{N}\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">whereas the best polynomial error decays only algebraically in <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence even piecewise-linear activations can be approximated to high accuracy with modest rational degree.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Practical consequences.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Coverage.</span> Eqs. equation <a href="#A2.E32" title="In Density on compact sets. ‣ Appendix B Why rational function? ‣ Don’t Forget the Nonlinearity: Unlocking Activation Functions in Efficient Fine-Tuning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>–equation <a href="#A2.E34" title="In Near-root-exponential rates for kinks. ‣ Appendix B Why rational function? ‣ Don’t Forget the Nonlinearity: Unlocking Activation Functions in Efficient Fine-Tuning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a> ensure a single rational family can approximate most activations used in deep learning on bounded pre-activation sets.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Efficiency.</span> The fast rates in equation <a href="#A2.E33" title="In Fast rates for smooth activations. ‣ Appendix B Why rational function? ‣ Don’t Forget the Nonlinearity: Unlocking Activation Functions in Efficient Fine-Tuning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">33</span></a>–equation <a href="#A2.E34" title="In Near-root-exponential rates for kinks. ‣ Appendix B Why rational function? ‣ Don’t Forget the Nonlinearity: Unlocking Activation Functions in Efficient Fine-Tuning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a> imply that low degrees suffice in practice, keeping parameters and compute small.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stability.</span> The pole-free margin equation <a href="#A2.E31" title="In Definition. ‣ Appendix B Why rational function? ‣ Don’t Forget the Nonlinearity: Unlocking Activation Functions in Efficient Fine-Tuning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a> ensures bounded slopes/curvatures on <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, making training numerically stable while retaining expressive shape control via the coefficients.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Experiment Details</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The tables <a href="#A3.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ Appendix C Experiment Details ‣ Don’t Forget the Nonlinearity: Unlocking Activation Functions in Efficient Fine-Tuning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> and table <a href="#A3.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ Appendix C Experiment Details ‣ Don’t Forget the Nonlinearity: Unlocking Activation Functions in Efficient Fine-Tuning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> below show the hyperparameter during tuning the models.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T7" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 7: </span>Hyperparameter settings for training ViT-Tiny on CIFAR-100.</figcaption>
<table id="A3.T7.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A3.T7.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T7.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="A3.T7.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hyperparameter</span></th>
<th id="A3.T7.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A3.T7.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Value</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A3.T7.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T7.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">Input resolution</th>
<td id="A3.T7.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><math id="A3.T7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="224^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>224</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">224^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T7.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T7.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Epochs</th>
<td id="A3.T7.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">50</td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T7.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T7.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Batch size</th>
<td id="A3.T7.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">256</td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T7.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T7.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Learning rate</th>
<td id="A3.T7.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A3.T7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times 10^{-3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times 10^{-3}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T7.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T7.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Learning rate decay</th>
<td id="A3.T7.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Cosine</td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T7.2.7" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T7.2.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Optimizer</th>
<td id="A3.T7.2.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">AdamW</td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T7.2.8" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T7.2.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Weight decay</th>
<td id="A3.T7.2.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">0.05</td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T7.2.9" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T7.2.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">AMP</th>
<td id="A3.T7.2.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">True</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.T8" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 8: </span>Hyperparameter settings for instruct tuning.</figcaption>
<table id="A3.T8.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A3.T8.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T8.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="A3.T8.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hyperparameter</span></th>
<th id="A3.T8.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A3.T8.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Value</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A3.T8.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T8.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">Cutoff length</th>
<td id="A3.T8.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">1024</td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T8.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T8.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Flash attention</th>
<td id="A3.T8.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">auto</td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T8.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T8.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Max new tokens</th>
<td id="A3.T8.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">512</td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T8.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T8.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Max samples</th>
<td id="A3.T8.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">1000</td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T8.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T8.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Per-device eval batch size</th>
<td id="A3.T8.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">2</td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T8.2.7" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T8.2.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Preprocessing workers</th>
<td id="A3.T8.2.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">16</td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T8.2.8" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T8.2.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Quantization method</th>
<td id="A3.T8.2.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">bnb</td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T8.2.9" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T8.2.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Stage</th>
